ular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="10916_338545_1773033"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To store data in such a way that it can be retrieved later by the same security support component, and only by that security support component.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="338545">seal</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="qut-GT"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1773033">uk'olik cholajil</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GTM</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="10928_359996_2314840"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A table, query, form, report, macro, or module that remains in the replica or Design Master where it was created. Neither the object nor changes to the object are copied to other members in the replica set.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="359996">local object</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="qut-GT"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2314840">jastaq ajwaral</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GTM</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="10934_237291_1906861"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An option that applies a read-only state to a document inside client applications.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="237291">Mark as Final</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalN