 used in some programming languages, notably C, to declare variables that can store floating-point numbers.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1520">float</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="qut-GT"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1596141">float</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GTM</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="11330_360145_2314929"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A program you use to view, print, and electronically mail a snapshot, such as a report snapshot.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="360145">Snapshot Viewer</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="qut-GT"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2314929">Ilol rech kemk'olib'al aninaqil</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GTM</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1134_36967_1595997"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To reduce the size of a set of data, such as a file or a communications message, so that it can be stored in less space or transmitted with less bandwidth.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="36967">compress</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="qut-GT"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1595997">t'ajinik</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GTM</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNo