a that follows a pattern or that is based on data in other cells.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="752822">Auto Fill</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="qut-GT"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2678356">Nojisab'al pa utukelam</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GTM</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="20867_752822_2678357"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The feature that allows the user to fill cells with data that follows a pattern or that is based on data in other cells.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="752822">Auto Fill</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="qut-GT"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2678357">Nojisab'alpautukelam</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GTM</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2087_22056_1806940"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A page where there is no information displayed</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="22056">blank page</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="qut-GT"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1806940">Uxaq jamalik</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GTM</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="20874_757176_1907105"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A tool used to turn on language-specific options for the languages one wants to use with a product.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="757176">Language Settings tool</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="qut-GT"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1907105">chakub'al rech uwiqitajem le ch'ab'al</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GTM</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="20884_759071_1596484"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Any hardware or software that can detect events or environmental changes, such as your current location or the amount of light around your computer. For example, a notebook with a location sensor, such as a Global Positioning System (GPS) receiver, can determine your exact location. An ambient light sensor can detect when there is a change in lighting, and then a program can use that information to adjust the brightness of your screen.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="759071">sensor</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="qut-GT"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1596484">repretib'al</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GTM</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="20888_759108_1596173"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A device that includes an antenna, a radio receiver, and a processor for use with the worldwide GPS (Global Positioning System). A GPS receiver uses position and time information from four GPS satellites to calculate precise information about its current location, its speed of travel, and the current time.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="759108">GPS receiver</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="qut-GT"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1596173">k'ulanel rech GPS</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GTM</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="20889_759109_1772981"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A category of sensor that can detect the current location of your computer.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="759109">location sensor</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="qut-GT"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1772981">repretib'al rech k'olib'al</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GTM</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="20907_759640_1772980"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An area within the Windows Control Panel that provides support for sensors such as enabling, disabling or uninstalling sensors and sensor-enabled applications, changing sensor settings, etc.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="759640">Location and Other Sensors</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="qut-GT"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1772980">Repretib'al rech k'olib'al chi'l nik'aj taq repretib'al</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GTM</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2091_50057_1596095"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A unit of information within a markup language that is defined by a tag, or a pair of tags surrounding some content, and includes any attributes defined within the initial tag.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="50057">element</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="qut-GT"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1596095">kemtz'aqatil</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GTM</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="20916_759739_1596578"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An arrangement of search results ordered by relevance using a special search algorithm.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="759739">top results</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="qut-GT"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1596578">je'l uwach chak</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GTM</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="20959_1167313_1596316"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A single set of sign-in credentials (typically, email address and password) that is used to access the services provided by an online service provider (OSP).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1167313">Web account</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="qut-GT"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1596316">rajaw upatanib'al chak</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GTM</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="20959_760161_1596316"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A single set of sign-in credentials (typically, email address and password) that is used to access the services provided by an online service provider (OSP).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="760161">online account</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="qut-GT"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1596316">rajaw upatanib'al chak</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GTM</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="20959_776387_1596316"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A single set of sign-in credentials (typically, email address and password) that is used to access the services provided by an online service provider (OSP).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="776387">online identity</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</te