 public services through email, social media and public cloud. It includes encryption of enterprise data when it enters the device or is created on the device, such that data stays protected against disclosure to applications and endpoints outside enterprise control.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2405212">Windows Information Protection</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="qut-GT"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2353933">Chajinem rech taq juq'attzij k'aywokaj</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GTM</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="40497_2405212_2413271"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The feature set that integrates data protection at the platform level so as to protect corporate data against inadvertent disclosure to unauthorized users and public services through email, social media and public cloud. It includes encryption of enterprise data when it enters the device or is created on the device, such that data stays protected against disclosure to applications and endpoints outside enterprise control.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2405212">Windows Information Protection</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="qut-GT"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2413271">Chajib'al q'alajisanem rech Windows</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GTM</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="4050_95643_1596400"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A standard set of formats and procedures that enable computers to exchange information.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="95643">protocol</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="qut-GT"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1596400">cholk'utchak</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GTM</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="40502_2353112_2353934"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The app that consumers can use to send feedback to the Windows team, to check for responses to that feedback, and to get news about the latest updates.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2353112">Windows Feedback Hub</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="qut-GT"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2353934">Utzijoxik Hub</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GTM</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="40502_2353112_2353936"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The app that consumers can use to send feedback to the Windows team, to check for responses to that feedback, and to get news about the latest updates.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2353112">Windows Feedback Hub</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="qut-GT"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2353936">Utzijoxik Hub rech Windows</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GTM</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="40502_2353113_2353934"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The app that consumers can use to send feedback to the Windows team, to check for responses to that feedback, and to get news about the latest updates.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2353113">Feedback Hub</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="qut-GT"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2353934">Utzijoxik Hub</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GTM</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="40502_2353113_2353936"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The app that consumers can use to send feedback to the Windows team, to check for responses to that feedback, and to get news about the latest updates.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2353113">Feedback Hub</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="qut-GT"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2353936">Utzijoxik Hub rech Windows</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GTM</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="40503_2353114_2353932"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A group of settings that admins can use to manage files and operating system settings on enterprise-owned devices.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2353114">enterprise control</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="qut-GT"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2353932">ilawachib’al k’aywokaj</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GTM</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="40504_2353123_2353935"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The modern implementation of Windows PowerShell built on .NET Core. It includes a command-line shell, scripting language, and automation engine, providing IT administrators comprehensive control and automation of system administration tasks across multiple platforms.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2353123">PowerShell Core</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="qut-GT"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2353935">PowerShell Core</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GTM</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="4055_21561_1595915"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The smallest unit of information handled by a computer or device. One bit expresses a 1 or a 0 in a binary numeral, or a true or false logical condition. A group of 8 bits makes up a byte, which can represent many types of information, such as a letter of the alphabet, a decimal digit, or other character.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="21561">bit</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="qut-GT"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1595915">bit</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GTM</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="4055_21562_1595915"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The smallest unit of information handled by a computer or device. One bit expresses a 1 or a 0 in a binary numeral, or a true or false logical condition. A group of 8 bits makes up a byte, which can represent many types of information, such as a letter of the alphabet, a decimal digit, or other character.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="21562">binary digit</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="qut-GT"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1595915">bit</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GTM</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="4059_124417_1906533"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A file (or component within another file) that contains Automation standard descriptions of exposed objects, properties, and methods.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="124417">type library</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="qut-GT"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1906533">ucholajil k'olno'j kemchak</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GTM</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termN