 with the community in activities such as listening and responding to customer feedback, contributing to community forums, blogging about tips and tricks, and more.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2375041">community champion</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="qut-GT"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2379203">k'amal b'e rech wokaj</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GTM</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="41957_2751151_2379203"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A person who informally represents their feature team by sharing their expertise with the community in activities such as listening and responding to customer feedback, contributing to community forums, blogging about tips and tricks, and more.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2751151">community champ</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="qut-GT"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2379203">k'amal b'e rech wokaj</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GTM</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="4197_113668_1596511"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A power-saving state that allows the computer or device to quickly resume full-power operation (typically within several seconds) when you want to start working again. All open documents and programs are saved to memory before the computer or device enters the low-power state.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="113668">sleep</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="qut-GT"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1596511">uxlanem</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GTM</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="4197_312080_1596511"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A power-saving state that allows the computer or device to quickly resume full-power operation (typically within several seconds) when you want to start working again. All open documents and programs are saved to memory before the computer or device enters the low-power state.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="312080">sleep mode</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="qut-GT"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1596511">uxlanem</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GTM</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="41978_2375534_2379206"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The nickname for Windows 10, version 1607​, used by marketing and executives in announcements about this update, but not in the product.​</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2375534">Windows 10 Anniversary Update</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="qut-GT"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2379206">K'ak'arisab'al uq'ijol Windows 10</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GTM</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="42013_2376461_2381557"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The grouping of similar apps together on the taskbar.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2376461">glomming</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="qut-GT"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2381557">molajil kojkemchak</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GTM</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="42014_2376761_2382998"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The ribbon tab that gives users a set of options for editing graphics in their PowerPoint slides, Word documents, and Excel documents.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2376761">Graphics Tools</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="qut-GT"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2382998">Taq chakub'al rech k'utwachib'al</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GTM</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="42015_2376763_2382989"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The feature that allows users to replace a graphic with a different one.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2376763">Change Graphic</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalN